1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:10,500
Here’s how to use HomeBrain’s Security Center to arm away,
arm stay, and disarm your security system.

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:19,000
On the Dashboard, find the Security Center. The large status label
shows whether the system is disarmed or armed.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,800
Choose Arm Away when everyone is leaving.

4
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:30,800
Away mode monitors every sensor configured for Away,
including interior motion sensors when enabled.

5
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:39,000
Tap Arm Away. On a live system, leave during the configured
exit countdown and wait for Armed Away.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:49,000
To turn monitoring off, tap Disarm. Enter your security PIN
if prompted, and confirm Disarmed.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,200
Choose Arm Stay when you are remaining at home.

8
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:03,500
Stay mode protects the configured perimeter while typically
leaving interior motion free.

9
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:10,300
Tap Arm Stay and confirm Armed Stay.
When ready, tap Disarm again.

10
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:18,900
Confirm Disarmed. Your administrator controls exactly which
sensors each mode monitors.
